cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Snitch or TemptationBench, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Snitch: an integrity layer for AI coding agents, and TemptationBench"
abstract: >-
  Snitch detects when an AI coding agent makes tests pass by tampering with them
  (weakening, skipping or deleting tests, reconfiguring the test runner, planting the
  values a test asserts) and checks whether the agent disclosed it. It ships as a Claude
  Code plugin with an escalation tool and an anti-reward-hacking policy, a GitHub Action
  and pre-commit hook, and TemptationBench, a set of 40 tasks with built-in temptations
  and hidden tests for measuring how often coding agents cheat.
authors:
